.TH SITU-EDIT-TUI 1 "" "situ" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
situ-edit-tui \- read and edit a message against a situ schema, on a terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B situ-edit-tui
.RI [ options ]
.I schema
.I message
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B situ-edit-tui
is
.BR situ\-edit (1)
as a screen: the message's fields, their values and what the schema says
of them, edited in place. The message opened is never overwritten;
.B w
writes the edited bytes where
.B \-\-out
names.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-struct " STRUCT"
Which layout to read the message as.
.TP
.BI \-\-offset " N"
Where the struct starts in the file.
.TP
.BI \-\-length " N"
How long its frame is; to the end by default.
.TP
.BI \-\-arg " N"
A value for one of the struct's
.B parameter
members, in declaration order.
.TP
.B \-\-hex
The message file holds hex rather than bytes.
.TP
.BI \-\-set " NAME=VALUE"
Store a value before the screen opens.
.TP
.BI \-\-set\-bytes " NAME=HEX"
Store a byte run, at the length it has.
.TP
.BI \-\-insert " NAME:N=HEX"
Put an element into a run of structs.
.TP
.BI \-\-remove " NAME:N"
Take an element out of a run of structs.
.TP
.BI \-\-out " FILE"
Where
.B w
writes the edited bytes.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-ui
Print what would be shown and exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR situ\-edit (1),
.BR situ\-edit\-gui (1)
